course: dictionary
lesson: 11026
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and wax is one of them. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it: that is its context.
explain: «Bees turn flower nectar into honey and store it in six-sided wax cells.» Here wax is a material that bees make, so it means the soft stuff that melts when warm. Try that meaning in the sentence: cells made of soft stuff makes sense.
explain: «The moon waxes, looking bigger each night.» Here wax is an action word, so the moon is doing something. The clues are the moon and each night. Always ask: is this word a thing or something you do? That tells you which meaning to try.
fact: Wax is a soft material that melts when warm.
fact: «Candle wax» and «beeswax» are two kinds of wax you may meet.
fact: To wax something means to rub wax on it to make it shiny or smooth, like a car or a floor.
fact: «Earwax» is the soft yellow stuff in your ears.
fact: Wax can also be an action word: the moon waxes when it looks bigger each night.
exercise: «Wax crayons are made of melted coloured wax poured into moulds.» What is wax here? | To rub something to make it shiny | A bright colour | *A soft material that melts when warm | A kind of paper label
exercise: Dad says, «I will wax the car this weekend.» What does wax mean? | *To rub wax on something to make it shiny | To melt something in a pan | To count money slowly | To clean out your ears
exercise: «The moon waxes each night.» What is the moon doing when it waxes? | Turning into candle wax | Falling down into the sea | *Looking bigger each night | Going out for good
test: What is the wax in «Bees make wax for their honeycomb»? | *A soft material made by bees | A kind of honey | A bright lamp | To shine a floor
test: Can wax be an action word? | No, wax is only ever a thing | No, wax only means the stuff in your ears | *Yes, as in «to wax a floor» or «the moon waxes»
exam: Which meaning of wax fits «The moon waxes, looking bigger each night»? | Soft material that melts when warm | *To grow bigger, as the moon does | To polish a car | Yellow stuff in your ears
